    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d246">

                <pb facs="0693" n="1507" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v02p2/pg1507"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Eisenhower Library, Whitman file, “AEC”</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the United States Atomic Energy
                        Commission (Strauss) to the President</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-09-03">September 3, 1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>: The purpose of this letter
                    is to request your authorization, in accordance with Section 144a of the Atomic
                    Energy Act of 1954,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d246-f1"/> to continue to cooperate
                    with Canada and the United Kingdom in the exchange of Restricted Data in certain
                    areas pursuant to agreements existing on the effective date of the Act.</p>
                <p>Attached is a statement concerning the statutory basis for the requested
                    authorization and a description of the type of information exchanged under
                    existing programs.</p>
                <p>In summary, authorization is requested for the continuance of the following
                    programs of cooperation: <pb facs="0694" n="1508" xml:id="pg1508"/>
                    <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>The program of Technical Cooperation (excluding the area entitled
                            “Detection of Distant Nuclear Explosions”) and the program of Raw
                            Materials Cooperation among the United States, the United Kingdom, and
                            Canada. This cooperation is pursuant to a <hi rendition="#italic">Modus
                                Vivendi</hi> dated January 7, 1948, adopted by the three
                                governments.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d246-f2"/></item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Cooperation with Canada on uranium refining processes and technology,
                            pursuant to an arrangement approved by the President on January 17,
                                1952,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d246-f3"/> in accordance with Section
                            10(a) (3) of the Atomic Energy Act of 1946, as amended.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Cooperation with the United Kingdom in connection with the exchange of
                            certain intelligence information, pursuant to an arrangement approved by
                            the President on June 26, 1952,<anchor n="4" xml:id="d246-f4"/> in
                            accordance with Section 10(a) (3) of the Atomic Energy Act of 1946, as
                            amended.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>Cooperation with Canada in a joint program for the development of
                            reactor fuel elements, pursuant to an arrangement approved by the
                            President on July 13, 1953, in accordance with Section 10(a) (3) of the
                            Atomic Energy Act of 1946, as amended.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Your authorization of the continuance of the foregoing programs of cooperation is
                        recommended.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d246-f5"/></p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>[<signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lewis
                                L. Strauss</hi></signed>]</closer>


                <xi:include href="d246-a1.xml" xpointer="d246-a1"/>
